<usx version="3.1">
<book code="PHM" style="id">BLB-Draft</book>

<para style="h">Philemon</para>

<para style="toc1">Philemon</para>

<para style="rem">sourceUrl=https://literalbible.com/blb.docx fetchedAtUtc=2026-09-01T15:43:00Z status=draft id=BLB-Draft spec=USFM-USX 3.1.1 char:add=docx-italic note:f=docx-footnotes note:x=docx-heading-crossrefs</para>

<chapter number="1" style="c" sid="PHM 1"/>

<para style="s">Greetings from Paul and Timothy</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PHM 1:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Colossians 1:1–2</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Philippians 1:1–2</char></note>Paul, a prisoner of Christ Jesus,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> F35 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Jesus Christ</char></note> and Timothy the brother, To Philemon, our beloved and fellow worker, <verse eid="PHM 1:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PHM 1:2"/>and to Apphia the sister,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">our sister</char></note> and to Archippus our fellow soldier, and to the church at your<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">You</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> and </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Your</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> are singular throughout this letter, except in verses 3, 22, and 25.</char></note> house: <verse eid="PHM 1:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PHM 1:3"/>Grace to you⁺ and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ. <verse eid="PHM 1:3"/></para>

<para style="s">Philemon’s Faith and Love</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PHM 1:4"/>I thank my God always, making remembrance of you in my prayers, <verse eid="PHM 1:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PHM 1:5"/>hearing of your love and the faith that you have toward the Lord Jesus and for all the saints, <verse eid="PHM 1:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PHM 1:6"/>so that the fellowship of your faith might become effective in the full knowledge of every good <char style="add">thing</char> that <char style="add">is</char> in us in Christ.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in Christ Jesus</char></note> <verse eid="PHM 1:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PHM 1:7"/>For I have<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">we have</char></note> much joy and encouragement on the basis of your love, because the inner parts of the saints have been refreshed by you, brother. <verse eid="PHM 1:7"/></para>

<para style="s">Paul’s Appeal for Onesimus</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PHM 1:8"/>Therefore, having much boldness in Christ to order you <char style="add">to do</char> what <char style="add">is</char> fitting, <verse eid="PHM 1:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PHM 1:9"/>because of love, rather, I exhort <char style="add">you</char>, being such a one as Paul, now an elderly man and also a prisoner of Christ Jesus.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of Jesus Christ</char></note> <verse eid="PHM 1:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PHM 1:10"/>I exhort you concerning my child whom I begot in chains,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in my chains</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> Onesimus,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Onesimus</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">useful</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> (see verse 11) or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">beneficial</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> (see verse 20).</char></note> <verse eid="PHM 1:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PHM 1:11"/>the one once useless to you, but now useful both to you and to me, <verse eid="PHM 1:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PHM 1:12"/>whom I sent back to you himself—this <char style="add">one who</char> is my inner parts— <verse eid="PHM 1:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PHM 1:13"/>whom I was wishing to keep with myself, so that on behalf of you he might minister to me in the chains of the gospel. <verse eid="PHM 1:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PHM 1:14"/>But apart from your consent I wanted to do nothing, so that your good may be not as according to necessity, but according to willingness. <verse eid="PHM 1:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PHM 1:15"/>For perhaps because of this he was separated for an hour, so that you might have him back eternally, <verse eid="PHM 1:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PHM 1:16"/>no longer as a slave, but above a slave, a beloved brother—especially to me, but how much more to you, both in the flesh and in the Lord. <verse eid="PHM 1:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PHM 1:17"/>Therefore, if you hold me a partner, receive him as me. <verse eid="PHM 1:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PHM 1:18"/>But if in any way he wronged you or he owes <char style="add">you</char>, impute this to me. <verse eid="PHM 1:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PHM 1:19"/>I, Paul, wrote with my own hand. I will repay <char style="add">it</char>, that I may not say to you that you also owe to me even yourself. <verse eid="PHM 1:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PHM 1:20"/>Yes, brother, may I have profit<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Greek </char><char style="fq" closed="false">onaimēn</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, a play on the name </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Onesimus</char></note> from you in the Lord. Refresh my inner parts in Christ.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in the Lord</char></note> <verse eid="PHM 1:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PHM 1:21"/>Being persuaded of your obedience, I wrote to you, knowing that you will do even above what I say. <verse eid="PHM 1:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PHM 1:22"/>Now at the same time, also prepare a lodging for me; for I hope that through your⁺ prayers I will be graciously given to you⁺. <verse eid="PHM 1:22"/></para>

<para style="s">Additional Greetings</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PHM 1:23"/>Epaphras, my fellow prisoner in Christ Jesus, greets you, <verse eid="PHM 1:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PHM 1:24"/><char style="add">as do</char> Mark, Aristarchus, Demas, <char style="add">and</char> Luke, my fellow workers. <verse eid="PHM 1:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PHM 1:25"/>The grace of the Lord Jesus Christ<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of our Lord Jesus Christ</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; F35 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of our Lord Jesus</char></note> <char style="add">be</char> with your⁺ spirit.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Amen.</char></note> <verse eid="PHM 1:25"/></para>

<chapter eid="PHM 1"/>

</usx>
